  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1240 PM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nFriday...The high amplitude ridge axis aloft moves from western \nWyoming to western Nebraska by evening, with subsidence and dry air \ncontinuing the dry and mild trends. 700 mb temperatures near 5 \nCelsius will yield high temperatures from the mid 50s to mid 60s.\n\nSaturday...The flow aloft turns southerly with falling heights as \nthe next trough aloft approaches from the Great Basin states. Looks \nlike adequate low and mid level moisture to produce scattered \ndynamic and orographic showers across our Snowy and Sierra Madre \nRanges, with dry conditions elsewhere. Cooler temperatures with more \nopaque cloud cover overhead.\n\nSunday...The trough aloft opens up and moves into the Texas \nPanhandle by late in the day, with only some residual cloud cover, \nand no precipitation left over in our forecast area.\n\nMonday...Another transitory ridge aloft moves overhead, keeping our \nweather dry and mild, with 700 mb temperatures trends suggesting \nslightly warmer surface temperatures.\n\nTuesday...The flow aloft backs to south southwesterly in advance of \nthe next approaching shortwave trough aloft. Looks like enough low \nand mid level moisture for scattered rain and snow showers over much \nof Carbon County, including the Sierra Madre Range, with dry \nconditions elsewhere. Temperatures slightly cooler with additional \ncloud cover compared to Monday.",
